title    Seven Eighths Fusion (trio seven revision)
composer Claude
about    Revision of the 7/8 fusion loop toward a swung jazz-trio seven, over the same Dm11, Bbmaj13#11, Gm9 and altered A7.

# Feedback: "fusion 7 feels lame. make it like mehldau all the things we are 7 feel?"
#
# How the note is read: Brad Mehldau's trio version of All the Things You Are
# is in 7/4 and played as a swinging acoustic trio, with walking bass, ride
# cymbal time, piano comping and long right-hand lines that run across the bar
# line. The original loop is the opposite of that: straight sixteenths, a rock
# kick/snare backbeat, epiano stabs on every group start and a string pad, so the
# 7 is announced as a riff. The revision keeps the four chords and their exact
# voicings, and keeps 2+2+3 as the grouping, but makes the seven swing and flow.
#
# What changed and why:
# - Meter: 7/8 in sixteenths becomes 7/4 in swung eighths (beats 7, steps 2,
#   swing 0.28). The reference is a quarter-note seven, and swing only means
#   something on eighths against a quarter pulse. 2+2+3 now groups quarters.
# - Tempo: quarter = 120 is kept, which was the original reading of "about
#   120 bpm". Each bar is now twice as long (7 quarters instead of 7 eighths).
# - Sound: epiano and strings become acoustic piano, ebass becomes upright, and
#   the kick/snare/hat backbeat becomes ride-cymbal time. The pad is dropped,
#   because a held string pad reads as fusion, not trio.
# - Phrasing: comping hits move off the beat (the "and"s) and anticipate the
#   next group or bar, instead of stabbing every group start. A right-hand line
#   is added that ties across bar lines, so the bar line stops being audible
#   while the 2+2+3 grouping is still carried by the ride accents, hi-hat foot
#   and bass contour.
# - Drums vary from bar to bar instead of repeating with %, so it sounds played.
tempo    120
beats    7
steps    2
swing    0.28

# One bar = 7 quarters x 2 swung eighths = 14 steps. Group starts (2+2+3) fall
# on steps 0, 4, 8, which are beats 1, 3, 5.

# Piano left hand: the original rootless voicings, unchanged in pitch.
voice lh piano vol=0.6 pan=-0.15
# Piano right hand: single-note line above the voicings.
voice rh piano vol=0.8 pan=-0.15
voice bass upright vol=1.0 gate=0.9 pan=0.1
voice ride ride vol=0.6 pan=0.2
voice hat hat vol=0.4
voice snare snare vol=0.45
voice kick kick vol=0.45

pattern A
# Left hand comp, all on offbeats or anticipations:
# bar 1 Dm11 on the "and" of 2 and the "and" of 6; bar 2 Bbmaj13#11 on 1, then
# the "and" of 4 pushing into the 3-group; bar 3 Gm9 on 2, then the "and" of 4
# held through the 3-group; bar 4 Gm9 on 1, then A7alt (G C# F Bb C) pushed to
# the "and" of 4 and restruck on the "and" of 6, resolving to Dm11.
lh | .-- F3+C4+E4+G4+A4--- .--- F3+C4+E4+G4+A4-- | A3+D4+E4+G4---- .- A3+D4+E4+G4-- .--- | .- Bb3+D4+F4+A4- .-- Bb3+D4+F4+A4------ | Bb3+D4+F4+A4--- .-- G3+C#4+F4+Bb4+C5-- . G3+C#4+F4+Bb4+C5-- |
# Right hand line in swung eighths. Bar 1 climbs the Dm11 (A C E G) and leaves
# E5 on the last "and", tied into bar 2 where it becomes the #11 of Bb. Bar 2
# outlines Bb lydian (D E G A) and breathes. Bar 3 runs up Gm9 and leads into
# bar 4, where C#5 anticipates A7alt on the "and" of 4 and the line climbs the
# altered scale (Bb C Eb G) so G5 falls to F5, the third of Dm, at the loop.
rh | F5-- . A4 C5 E5 G5 F5- D5 C5 . E5 | --- D5 E5 G5 A5- G5 E5 D5 .-- | .- Bb4 D5 F5 A5 G5- F5 D5 Bb4 A4 Bb4 C5 | D5--- . F5 E5 C#5-- Bb4 C5 Eb5 G5 |
# Walking bass in quarters with chromatic approaches into each new root
# (B1 to Bb1, Ab2 to G2, F#1 to G1, Eb2 to D2). One swung eighth skip in bar 3.
# In bar 4 the bass lands A1 on beat 5, the start of the 3-group, as before.
bass | D2- F2- A2- C3- D3- A2- B1- | Bb1- C2- D2- E2- F2- A2- Ab2- | G2- F2- D2- Bb1 A1 C2- D2- F#1- | G1- Bb1- D2- Bb1- A1- G2- Eb2- |
# Ride: "ding ding-a" swing pattern, accented on the 2+2+3 group starts.
ride  | X.xx X.xx X.xx x. | X.xx X.xx X.xx x. | X.xx X.xx X.xx x. | X.xx X.xx X.x.xx |
# Hi-hat foot on the second beat of each group (beats 2, 4, 6).
hat   | ..x. ..x. ..x... | % | % | % |
# Snare: sparse ghost-note comping that answers the piano, plus a short
# pickup in bar 4 into the loop point.
snare | o... ...o ..o... | .... .o.. ...x.. | ..o. ...o ....o. | .... ...x .o.oxX |
# Kick: feathered quietly on group starts, with soft accents under the piano
# anticipations on the "and" of 4 in bars 2 and 4.
kick  | o... o... o..... | o... ...x o..... | o... o... o..... | o... ...x ...... |

loop A
